    "**Discussion 1d.** The calibrated amplitude is A = 0.200 ΔF/F per spike. This is the same single-spike amplitude used in the lecture model (`gen_calcium_transients(sp, kernel, 0.2)`), although because A trades off against the assumed firing rates it is not an independent measurement. Measured with the same estimator, the noise matches the real data (0.046 real against 0.047 for both surrogates), and the example traces look similar in scale and noise.\n",
